        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"from_meta\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"from_meta\"],\"handles\":[\"from_meta\"]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"from_meta\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"from_meta\"],\"handles\":[\"from_meta\"]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"from_meta\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"from_meta\"],\"handles\":[\"from_meta\"]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "MCP puts implementation data in `_meta`, so it is read first. A surface sending both is not a surface a package should have an opinion about — but the two languages that picked different ones would hand two agents different conversations."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0017",
      "title": "the top level is read when `_meta` has nothing to say",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"changes\":[{\"screen_id\":\"s1\",\"change\":\"created\"}],\"complete\":true}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"created\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"created\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"created\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "The fallback, pinned so it cannot quietly stop working. A surface with no `_meta` at all is the common shape outside MCP."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0018",
      "title": "spellings are matched case-insensitively and trimmed",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"changes\":[{\"screen_id\":\"s1\",\"change\":\"  MOVED  \",\"actor_type\":\"Human\"}]}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"attributed\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":true,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"human\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"attributed\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":true,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"human\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"attributed\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":true,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"s1\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"human\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"s1\"],\"handles\":[\"s1\"]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "Surfaces are written by people. Matching only the exact lowercase token would make this row `unknown`/`unknown` and silently stop deferring to a person's edit — the failure mode being guarded against, reached through capitalisation."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0019",
      "title": "a `changes` value that is not a list yields no rows rather than a crash",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"changes\":{\"screen_id\":\"s1\",\"change\":\"updated\"}}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "A hostile or broken surface sending an object where a list belongs must not take the turn down, and must not be read as one change either. The answer is an empty list from a feed that answered — which is exactly why `complete` and `answered` are separate from the list itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0020",
      "title": "handles are de-duplicated and keep first-seen order",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"changes\":[{\"screen_id\":\"b\",\"change\":\"updated\"},{\"screen_id\":\"a\",\"change\":\"moved\"},{\"screen_id\":\"b\",\"change\":\"moved\"}]}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"a\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"b\",\"a\",\"b\"],\"handles\":[\"b\",\"a\"]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"a\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"b\",\"a\",\"b\"],\"handles\":[\"b\",\"a\"]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":false,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"updated\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"a\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"},{\"handle\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"moved\",\"actor\":\"unknown\",\"label\":\"\"}],\"defer_to\":[\"b\",\"a\",\"b\"],\"handles\":[\"b\",\"a\"]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "An agent re-reads by handle, so the list it re-reads from must not contain the same handle twice or arrive in an order that differs by language. Insertion order, not sorted: sorting would be this package inventing a priority the surface did not state."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0022",
      "title": "a FRACTIONAL revision is refused, because three languages cannot spell it alike",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"revision\":1.5,\"changes\":[]}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "The boundary the hpc-0021 fix creates, and the reason it stops where it does. A whole number is accepted however the host decoded it; a fractional one is refused in all three. Not because a surface may not mint `1.5` — markers are opaque — but because a marker that is not byte-identical in every language is worse than no marker: it is echoed back on the next call, and a surface enforcing the pin would refuse whichever agent spelled it differently. Refusing loudly in three languages beats agreeing in two."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0023",
      "title": "a revision beyond safe-integer range is refused rather than rounded",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"revision\":1e20,\"changes\":[]}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":null,\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "The other end of the same boundary. Past 2^53-1 the three languages stop agreeing on what the number even is — JavaScript has no integer wider than a double, PHP casts to a platform int, Python does not — so a counter that grew that large would be pinned to three different strings. Refused everywhere, at the same threshold, spelled as a literal in all three rather than as each language's own MAX."
    },
    {
      "id": "hpc-0021",
      "title": "an integral float revision, which is the G-35 shape in a new family",
      "since": "0.1.0",
      "input": {
        "result": "{\"_meta\":{\"revision\":1.0,\"changes\":[]}}",
        "feed": "offered"
      },
      "rows": {
        "php": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":\"1\",\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "ts": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":\"1\",\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}",
        "py": "{\"feed\":\"offered\",\"complete\":true,\"answered\":true,\"nothing_changed\":true,\"attributes\":false,\"revision\":\"1\",\"changes\":[],\"defer_to\":[],\"handles\":[]}"
      },
      "agrees": true,
      "notes": "`human-plus-tool-admission` G-35 records that an integral float digests as `1` in PHP and JavaScript and `1.0` in Python. A revision marker is compared as text and echoed back on every later call, so the same split here would mean two agents pinning the same surface state to two different strings — and a surface enforcing the pin would refuse one of them. Carried as raw text so the float survives into the test."
    }
  ]
